print request => #<curl-request>
curl-request-with no keys => "http://127.0.0.1:1/"
print engine => #<curl-engine>
print token => #<curl-token>
token-wait 0 => #t
print mailbox => #<curl-mailbox>
mailbox-take 0 => #f
print jar => #<curl-cookie-jar>
url eq copy? => #t
headers eq copy? => #t
header string eq copy? => #t
ca-file eq copy? => #t
user-agent eq copy? => #t
body bv eq copy? => #t
cancel => #f
await cancelled => (perform-failed 0)
jar read after close => RAISED (curl-request-error cookie-jar cookie-jar-closed)the cookie jar is closed, or closing: it takes no transfer, read-out or load more
second stop => #<void>
submit after stop => RAISED (curl-engine-error stopped)the engine was stopped, so it takes no more transfers
jar make on stopped => RAISED (curl-engine-error stopped)the engine was stopped, so it takes no more transfers
session cookies on no-cookie session => RAISED assertion the session keeps no cookies: make it with cookies #t
session cookie-beside-jar => RAISED (curl-request-error header-name cookie-beside-jar)a Cookie or Host header beside a cookie jar: libcurl would send a caller's Cookie beside the jar's, and match the jar's cookies against a caller's Host, sending and storing
session host beside jar => RAISED (curl-request-error header-name cookie-beside-jar)a Cookie or Host header beside a cookie jar: libcurl would send a caller's Cookie beside the jar's, and match the jar's cookies against a caller's Host, sending and storing
counts after refusal => ((block . 0) (easy . 0) (url . 0) (slist . 0) (curl-string . 0) (transfer . 0) (multi . 0) (share . 0) (mime . 0))
get with form => RAISED (http-request-error form body-not-allowed)a body, a form or a multipart body with get or head, which send none
get with multipart => RAISED (http-request-error multipart body-not-allowed)a body, a form or a multipart body with get or head, which send none
print session => "#<http-session>"
print retry => #<http-retry>
header beside call ua => 1
make-http-retry statuses 300 => RAISED (http-request-error statuses not-a-status-list)statuses is a list of exact integers from 400 to 599
redirects 0 session => #<http-session>
body-length 0 with stream => 0
stream-buffer 1 => 1
timeout 0 => RAISED assertion a timeout is a positive exact integer a long holds, or #f
body-limit 0 => 0
ca-file empty => RAISED assertion a CA file is a non-empty string, its path, or #f
ca-file pkcs11 => RAISED (curl-request-error ca-file pkcs11-url)a CA file's path that begins pkcs11:, in any ASCII case, is a PKCS#11 URL to GnuTLS, not a file; reach a file of that name as ./pkcs11:...
user-agent empty => RAISED assertion a user agent is a non-empty string or #f
header value VT => RAISED (curl-request-error header-value surrounding-whitespace)a header string starts or ends with whitespace, which libcurl trims
header value trailing tab => RAISED (curl-request-error header-value surrounding-whitespace)a header string starts or ends with whitespace, which libcurl trims
two Host => RAISED (curl-request-error header-name duplicates-field)a User-Agent header beside the user agent field, which libcurl would let win, or a second Host header, which libcurl would drop
UA header beside ua => RAISED (curl-request-error header-name duplicates-field)a User-Agent header beside the user agent field, which libcurl would let win, or a second Host header, which libcurl would drop
transfer-encoding => RAISED (curl-request-error header-name framing-header)a Content-Length or Transfer-Encoding header: libcurl frames the message, from the body it is handed
proxy-authorization => RAISED (curl-request-error header-name proxy-authorization-header)a Proxy-Authorization header: inside a tunnel libcurl sends it to the origin; give a proxy's credentials in its URL
credentials colon basic user => RAISED (curl-request-error credentials credentials-bytes)a credentials string holds a control char, U+0000 to U+001F or U+007F, which libcurl would write into its header unescaped, or a Basic user name holds a colon, where RFC 7617 ends the user
credentials colon digest user => (digest "a:b" "c")
credentials empty bearer => RAISED (curl-request-error credentials credentials-empty)credentials with nothing to send: a Bearer token, or a user and a password, that are all empty
credentials basic empty user only => (basic "" "p")
digest with stream-buffer => RAISED (curl-request-error credentials digest-with-stream)Digest credentials beside a streamed body or response: Digest makes a second request inside the transfer, which a stream cannot follow; Basic and Bearer send one
creds beside authorization => RAISED (curl-request-error credentials credentials-beside-authorization)credentials beside an Authorization header: libcurl would send one of the two, or both
url-error input string => (malformed-input 3)
url-part bad part => RAISED assertion not a part of a URL
url 8000001 ascii => (malformed-input 3)
